{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedSYTRoundTrip","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedSYTRoundTrip","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedRecordingOfSYT"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.sigma_listStandardYT_toListTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.sigma_listStandardYT_toListTableau","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedSYTRoundTrip.lean#L125-L131","doc":"**The bridge is an inverse.** Reading a standard Young tableau into the list representation and\nrealising it again returns the tableau — diagram and all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.sigma_ext_entry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.sigma_ext_entry","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedSYTRoundTrip.lean#L117-L123","doc":"Comparing tableaux on *different* diagrams: substitute the diagram, then compare entries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.shape_toListTableau_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.shape_toListTableau_eq","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedSYTRoundTrip.lean#L110-L115","doc":"The diagram the bridge lands on **is** `μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.ofRowLens_congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.ofRowLens_congr","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedSYTRoundTrip.lean#L105-L108","doc":"Equal row-length lists give equal diagrams; the sortedness proofs are irrelevant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_getD_toListTableau_all","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_getD_toListTableau_all","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedSYTRoundTrip.lean#L87-L103","doc":"**The list tableau reads back every entry** — on the diagram by construction, off it because\nboth sides are `0`: the list runs out, and a semistandard tableau vanishes off its shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.content_toListTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.content_toListTableau","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedSYTRoundTrip.lean#L69-L85","doc":"**The content of the bridged tableau is `{1, …, |μ|}`** — the hypothesis `listStandardYT` takes,\nin the multiset form it takes it. Both sides are duplicate-free with the same members. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.content_eq_flatten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.content_eq_flatten","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedSYTRoundTrip.lean#L62-L67","doc":"`content` is the flattening, as a multiset. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.ext_entry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.ext_entry","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedSYTRoundTrip.lean#L48-L52","doc":"**Extensionality by entries.** Two standard tableaux on the same diagram agreeing at every\nindex are equal — the `bijOn` fields are proofs, so they carry no extra data. ","signatureChunk":0}]}